 ## Background
-DreamFusion was introduced in September 2022 [S1][S4]. It was proposed as a text-to-3D diffusion NeRF model that uses images from 2D diffusion models (specifically Imagen) to train a NeRF from scratch [S1]. The method sidesteps the lack of large-scale 3D training datasets by optimizing a NeRF representation so that its multiview renderings match a given textual description, constrained by a 2D diffusion model used as a parametric prior [S2]. It introduced the Score Distillation Sampling (SDS) technique for this purpose [S2].
+*   **Origin:** DreamFusion was introduced in September 2022 [S1][S5].
+*   **Paper:** The method was proposed by Poole et al. [S3, unofficial] (referenced as [18] in [S2] and [85] in [S1]).
+*   **History:** It was a groundbreaking approach for text-to-3D synthesis that addressed the limitations of 3D data scarcity by introducing Score Distillation Sampling (SDS) [S4]. It built upon the NeRF framework and leveraged pretrained 2D diffusion models like Imagen [S1].
+*   **Usage:** It is used for text-to-3D generation and has inspired subsequent methods like Magic3D and Latent-NeRF [S1].
 
